{
  "name": "hauling-gate",
  "description": "Arrival-gated debris hauling (issue #437): 'vehicle haul <id> fragment:<id>' sets hauling intent only — a debris_hauler then drives to the blast fragment, loads it only on arrival, drives to the nearest freight_warehouse, and delivers it only on arrival. Immediately after the haul command (before the first post-command tick block), the fragment must still be on_ground/untransported — the state dump right after 'vehicle haul' proves the task did not start/complete instantly. After the first tick 20 the vehicle should be in transit (fragment picked up, hauling toward the depot) or already delivered; after the following tick 40 the fragment must be state:stored and logistics.storedMassKg increased.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:100000",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:100000"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 100000,
          "buildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build freight_warehouse at:5,5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"build\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"freight_warehouse\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 5,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "drill_plan grid rows:3 cols:3 spacing:3 depth:8 start:20,20",
      "description": "Corrected from the original rows:2 cols:2 spacing:5 (which command mode ran literally, producing 4 holes): the click drags the (20,20)-(25,25) rectangle at the Drill panel's own default spacing (DEFAULT_SPACING_M=3), computing cols/rows as round(size/spacing)+1 = 3x3 = 9 holes for that same rectangle -- the command and the click were silently testing two different grids, the same class of bug already fixed in nav-cell-types-visual.json. Caught by adding expect.equals.holeCount; fixed by describing what the click actually produces.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"blast\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"grid-tool\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "dragTiles",
          "x1": 20,
          "z1": 20,
          "x2": 25,
          "z2": 25
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "holeCount": 9
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "charge hole:* explosive:boomite amount:5 stemming:2",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"charge-all\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "chargedCount": 9
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "sequence auto delay_step:25",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"auto-sequence\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "sequencedCount": 9
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "blast",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"execute\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": ".bs-confirm-overlay .bs-btn-danger"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": ".bs-confirm-overlay .bs-btn-danger"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "[data-action=\"report-close\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "[data-action=\"report-close\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "holeCount": 0,
          "chargedCount": 0,
          "sequencedCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "fragments",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "fragments"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "storedMassKg": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "vehicle buy debris_hauler",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"vehicles\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-vehicle-panel [data-vtype=\"debris_hauler\"][data-tier=\"1\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-vehicle-panel [data-vtype=\"debris_hauler\"][data-tier=\"1\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "vehicleCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:driver",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"employees\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driver\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driver\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee assign_skill 1 skill:driving.truck level:1",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee assign_skill 1 skill:driving.truck level:1"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Left unmarked: hiring already grants the Rookie starting qualification (ROLE_STARTING_QUALIFICATION in Employee.ts); this only raises the level for the scenario's needs -- the player-facing path is `employee train`.",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 59200
        },
        "note": "the driver already holds driving.truck at level 1 from ROLE_STARTING_QUALIFICATION -- this call is a same-level no-op"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "vehicle driver 1 1",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"vehicles\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-vehicle-panel [data-vehicle-id=\"1\"] .bs-vehicle-assign-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-vehicle-panel [data-vehicle-id=\"1\"] .bs-vehicle-assign-btn"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 59200
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 10",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 10"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "storedMassKg": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "vehicle list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "vehicle list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "vehicle haul 1 fragment:531",
      "description": "The Haul button always picks the vehicle's nearest reachable, non-oversized, storage-fitting fragment (findReachableGroundFragment, HaulEligibility.ts) -- not a fixed index. #531 is what that function itself returns for this exact seed/command sequence (confirmed by calling it directly), which is why this id looks arbitrary rather than a round number picked by hand -- it must be re-derived the same way if anything upstream (the grid, the blast, the vehicle's spawn point) ever changes.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-vehicle-panel [data-vehicle-id=\"1\"] .bs-vehicle-haul-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-vehicle-panel [data-vehicle-id=\"1\"] .bs-vehicle-haul-btn"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 58620,
          "storedMassKg": 0
        },
        "note": "sets hauling intent only -- the fragment is not yet loaded, proving 'vehicle haul' does not complete instantly (#437)"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "fragments",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "fragments"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "storedMassKg": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 20",
      "description": "Confirmed via direct trace (seed:42) that the full pickup-drive-deliver cycle completes within this window -- storedMassKg is already at its final value by the end of this step, not just 'in transit'.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 20"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "increased": ["storedMassKg"]
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "fragments",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "fragments"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 40",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 40"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "note": "storedMassKg is deliberately not asserted to an exact value here: findReachableGroundFragment (the real Haul button's own fragment choice) is sensitive to the vehicle's exact tick-by-tick position, and interaction mode's real wall-clock ticking (Finding #12) can pick a different -- but equally valid -- fragment than command mode's clean tick10. The delivered amount genuinely differs between modes (confirmed: 263.25kg in command mode, 1050kg in a real browser run) without either being wrong; tick 20's own increased:[storedMassKg] check already proves delivery genuinely completed, which is this file's actual premise."
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "fragments",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "fragments"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1,
          "vehicleCount": 1,
          "buildingCount": 1
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
